CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!idtab"
#180: FILE: drivers/rapidio/rio-scan.c:908:
+		if (idtab == NULL) {

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*net)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct rio_net)...)
#263: FILE: drivers/rapidio/rio.c:101:
+	net = kzalloc(sizeof(struct rio_net), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

